{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Change 2656 pushed — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2656\n\nNot submitted, ticket left `in_progress`: the operator verifies votes and submits.\n\n### AC1 — the violator no longer allocates into the shared root\n\n`test_anthropic_lazy_import_isolation_heldout.py` now routes through `run_nested_pytest`.\nThe `python -c` payload's `assert 'pydantic_ai.providers.anthropic' not in sys.modules`\nwas dropped, and that loses nothing: it ran before `pytest.main`, in an interpreter that\nhad imported only `sys`, so it could not fail. A fresh `python -m pytest` child IS the\ncondition the test names.\n\nProof (run under an explicit parent `--basetemp`, so the module's children are the only\nthing that could have touched the shared root):\n\n```\n--- created ---   (none)\n--- DELETED ---   (none)\nchild basetemps:  .bt/ac1/test_anthropic_auth_oracle_iso{0,1,2,3}/nested-pytest\n```\n\n4 passed. Pre-fix the same module created four and deleted four.\n\n### AC2/AC3 — the guard, and the seeded defects\n\nThe guard no longer matches one argv shape. It classifies a sequence literal into three\nspellings of one operation and applies the admission each one can actually satisfy:\n\n| spelling | detection | admitted by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `python -m pytest` | argv triple `(sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pytest\")` | the helper, or a reasoned marker |\n| `python -c <payload naming pytest>` | `(sys.executable, \"-c\", payload)` where the payload's static text mentions pytest — resolved through the module's string bindings, since the violator bound its payload to a local first, and through f-string literal parts | the helper, or a reasoned marker |\n| bare `pytest` console script | argv[0] is `<anything> / \"pytest\"`, directly or via a local, through a `str()`/`os.fspath()` wrapper | an explicit `--basetemp` in the same literal, or a marker |\n\nThe console-script form gets the weaker admission on purpose: it *cannot* use the helper\n(`python -m pytest` puts the repo root on the child's `sys.path` and destroys what those\ntests reproduce), and the invariant being defended is the child's temp root, not the\nhelper's monopoly.\n\nDefect seeding, in the real tree, one spelling at a time — `test_the_launch_appears_only_in_the_helper`:\n\n```\nbaseline (all fixed)                          PASS\nseed 1: -c payload (the pre-fix violator)     FAIL\nseed 2: console script, --basetemp removed    FAIL\nseed 3: the -m triple (regression check)      FAIL\nrestored                                      PASS\n```\n\nFiles were set aside by copy under `git rev-parse --git-path heldout`, per the move\npattern in tasteful-euhedral-bilby — no stash was used anywhere.\n\nThe pre-fix payload is also kept verbatim in the guard as `_PRE_FIX_VIOLATOR`, so a\nrevert stays a permanently checked defect rather than one I checked once.\n\n### AC4 — the sweep, and its dispositions\n\nScanned: every `*.py` under `tests/` (the guard's own tree walk, which is the sweep) plus\na manual grep over `tests/`, `scripts/` and `src/` for `pytest.main`, quoted `pytest`,\n`Popen`/`check_output`/`check_call`, and every `\"-c\"` argv.\n\n| site | spelling | disposition |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_anthropic_lazy_import_isolation_heldout.py:32` | `-c` payload, no basetemp | **fixed here** (AC1) |\n| `test_tests_import_convention.py:97` | bare console script, **no basetemp** | **fixed here** — second violator, found by the widened guard, `--basetemp` added under `tmp_path` |\n| `test_scripts_import_convention.py:154` | bare console script | already passes `--basetemp`; admitted unchanged |\n| `test_mechanism_delta.py:440` | bare console script | already passes `--basetemp`; admitted unchanged |\n| `test_error_handling_convention.py:125`, `workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py:300`, `workflow/test_map_fanout.py:294`, `interfaces/facades/test_mcp_client_configs.py:365` | in-process `pytest.main` | all four are inside `if __name__ == \"__main__\":`, so they never run during a suite. Not flagged, deliberately. |\n| `test_ci_workflow_parity.py:1337` | `stub_bin / \"pytest\"` | a stub written to disk and put on `PATH`, never argv[0]. Correctly not flagged — verified. |\n| `test_caplog_coverage_integrity.py`, `test_repo_isolation_guard.py` | `pytester.runpytest*` | pytest owns their basetemp; out of scope, as `_nested_pytest.py` already records |\n| `scripts/run_live_matrix.py:80`, `scripts/mutation_gate.py:579` | build a pytest argv | outside `tests/`, so outside this guard's tree walk. **Not covered — see below.** |\n\nZero false positives: every other `python -c` payload under `tests/` (~12 sites) stays\nunflagged, and two negative-control tests pin that.\n\n### What the guard still cannot see — stated rather than claimed away\n\n- **Anything outside `tests/`.** `scripts/run_live_matrix.py` and `scripts/mutation_gate.py`\n  construct pytest argvs; the guard's tree walk is rooted at `tests/`. They are operator\n  tooling, not suite children, so they cannot prune a concurrent session's root the way a\n  test can — but the guard does not check them and I did not widen its root here.\n- **argv assembled incrementally** — `cmd = [sys.executable]` then `cmd += [\"-m\", \"pytest\"]`.\n  Detection is per sequence literal; no literal contains the triple. Not present in the\n  tree today.\n- **A console script not at argv[0]** — e.g. `[\"env\", \"X=1\", str(console_script), ...]`.\n  Only argv[0] is checked. Not present today.\n- **A `-c` payload that reaches pytest only through an interpolated value**, so no literal\n  part of the f-string says \"pytest\". Not present today.\n\nEach of these is a narrower gap than the one just closed, and each is listed so the next\nreader does not have to rediscover that it was a choice.\n\n### Gates and checks\n\n`make lint` rc=0; `make typecheck` rc=0 (762 files). Complexity ratchet `new=0 increased=0\nstale=16`; mechanism ratchet `new=0 increased=0`. No new mechanism was introduced — the\nchange reshapes an existing guard rather than adding one.\n\nVerified with the **bare `pytest` console script** throughout, not `python -m pytest`:\n`test_tests_import_convention.py` + `test_scripts_import_convention.py` green, and the\nfive affected modules green (57 passed).\n\n### One transient, recorded not chased\n\n`test_scripts_import_convention.py::test_repro_module_passes_standalone` failed once in a\nfour-module selection (child rc 1 with \"3 passed\" in its own output), then passed 4/4 on\nre-run with identical selection and `-p no:randomly`. That module is **unmodified by this\nchange**. Shape matches the same-family transient already noted in this ticket's\ndescription; not investigated further here.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788577647241659992,"uuid":"d0fbef30-f121-4ad8-96a5-1f3c8afa49f5"}